hild of Nozdormu. Destroy him and return his skull to Emberstrife.\03110321\03110321\0316570\031\03115\031classic-reference",[6585]="The Test of Skulls, Axtroz\031Travel to Grim Batol and track down Axtroz, drake champion of the Red Flight. Destroy him and take his skull. Return the skull to Emberstrife.\03110321\03110321\031\0316601\03115\031classic-reference",[659]="Hints of a New Plague?\031Find Quae and Kinelory near the Go'Shek Farm in the Arathi Highlands.\0312711\0312712\031\031658\031267\031classic-reference",[66]="The Legend of Stalvan\031Seek out the Clerk Daltry in the Darkshire Town Hall.\031265\031267\031\03167\03110\031classic-reference",[660]="Hints of a New Plague?\031Protect Kinelory until she returns to Quae.\0312713\0312712\031657\031661\031267\031classic-reference",[6601]="Ascension...\031It would appear as if the charade is over. You know that the Amulet of Draconic Subversion that Myranda the Hag created for you will not function inside Blackrock Spire. Perhaps you should find Rexxar and explain your predicament. Show him the Dull Drakefire Amulet. Hopefully he will know what to do next.\03110321\03110182\0316585\0316602\03115\031classic-reference",[6602]="Blood of the Black Dragon Champion\031Travel to Blackrock Spire and slay General Drakkisath. Gather his blood and return it to Rexxar.\03110182\03110182\0316601\031\0311583\031classic-reference",[6603]="Trouble in Winterspring!\031Find Donova Snowden near the hot springs in Winterspring.\03111754\0319298\031\0315082\031618\031classic-reference",[6604]="Enraged Wildkin\031Speak with Jaron Stoneshaper at Starfall Village.\03111755\03110301\031\0314861\031618\031classic-reference",[6605]="A Strange One\031Speak with Winna Hazzard in Felwood.\03111755\0319996\031\0314505\031618\031classic-reference",[6606]="A Little Luck\031Speak with Witch Doctor Mau'ari in Everlook.\03111755\03110307\031\031969\031618\031classic-reference",[6607]="Nat Pagle, Angler Extreme\031Nat Pagle wants you to catch the following fish:$B$BMisty Reed Mahi Mahi from the Misty Reed Strand in the Swamp of Sorrows.$B$BA Sar'theris Striker from the Sar'theris Strand in Desolace.$B$BFeralas Ahi from the Verdantis River of Feralas.$B$BSavage Coast Blue Sailfin from the Savage Coast of Stranglethorn Vale.$B$BReturn to Nat Pagle when you have reeled them all in!\03112919\03112919\031\031\031-101\031classic-reference",[6608]="You Too Good.\031You think Lumak is trying to tell you that he can no longer help you improve your fishing skill. You may want to try to find his friend, Nat Pagle, a human fishing off one of the islands south of Theramore (at least that's what you think Lumak said).\0313332\03112919\031\031\031-101\031classic-reference",[6609]="I Got Nothin' Left!\031Travel to Kalimdor, to the coastal city of Theramore. From there you must search for an island, south of the main town. Nat Pagle awaits your arrival!\0315161\03112919\031\031\031-101\031classic-reference",[661]="Hints of a New Plague?\031Find Phin Odelic in Southshore.\0312712\0312711\031660\031\031267\031classic-reference",[6610]="Clamlette Surprise\031Dirge Quikcleave wants you to get the following items:$B$B12 Giant Eggs. You will find those on the Rocs wandering Tanaris or any other species of large bird.$B$B10 pieces of Zesty Clam Meat. You can find those in clams, naturally!$B$B20 pieces of Alterac Swiss. Get thee to a cheesery!$B$BGather all of the items and return to Dirge.\0318125\0318125\031\031\031-304\031classic-reference",[6611]="To Gadgetzan You Go!\031Travel to Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert and speak with Dirge Quikcleave about advancing your cooking career.\0313399\0318125\031\0316610\031-304\031classic-reference",[6612]="I Know A Guy...\031Travel to Gadgetzan in the Tanaris desert and speak with Dirge Quikcleave about advancing your cooking career.$B\0315159\0318125\031\0316610\031-304\031classic-reference",[662]="Deep Sea Salvage\031First Mate Nilzlix wants you to retrieve the Charts and Logs from the Maiden's Folly and the Spirit of Silverpine.\0312767\0312767\031663\031\03145\031classic-reference",[6621]="King of the Foulweald\031Place Karang's Banner on the Foulweald Totem Mound.  Do not let the furbolgs destroy the banner.  Defeat Chief Murgut and bring Murgut's Totem to Karang Amakkar at Zoram'gar.\03112757\03112757\031216\031\031331\031classic-reference",[6622]="Triage\031Save patients by using Triage Bandages to tend to their wounds. You must save 15 patients before 6 of them die from their injuries.$B$BRemember the order of triage! Critically Injured Soldiers die the fastest followed by Badly Injured Soldiers. Injured Soldiers take the longest to die and should be saved AFTER your Critically Injured and Badly Injured Soldiers have been triaged.\03112920\03112920\031\031\031-324\031classic-reference",[6623]="Horde Trauma\031Travel to Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands and speak with Doctor Gregory Victor about joining the ranks of Horde Trauma.$B\0313373\03112920\031\0316622\031-324\031classic-reference",[6624]="Triage\031Save patients by using Triage Bandages to tend to their wounds. You must save 15 patients before 6 of them die from their injuries.$B$BRemember the order of triage! Critically Injured Soldiers die the fastest followed by Badly Injured Soldiers. Injured Soldiers take the longest to die and should be saved AFTER your Critically Injured and Badly Injured Soldiers have been triaged.\03112939\03112939\031\031\031-324\031classic-reference",[6625]="Alliance Trauma\031Travel to Theramore in the Dustwallow Marsh and speak with Doctor Gustaf VanHowzen about joining the ranks of Alliance Trauma.\0315150\03112939\031\0316624\031-324\031classic-reference",[6626]="A Host of Evil\031Kill 8 Razorfen Battleguard, 8 Razorfen Thornweavers, and 8 Death's Head Cultists and return to Myriam Moonsinger near the entrance to Razorfen Downs.\03112866\03112866\031\031\031722\031classic-reference",[6627]="Test of Lore\031Answer Braug Dimspirit's question successfully a