f Wood Pulp, and 6 samples of Sodium Nitrate.\0313341\0313341\031843\031849\03117\031classic-reference",[8460]="Timbermaw Ally\031Grazle wants you to prove yourself by killing 6 Deadwood Warriors, 6 Deadwood Pathfinders, and 6 Deadwood Gardeners.  Return to him in southern Felwood near the Emerald Sanctuary when you are done.\03111554\03111554\031\031\031361\031classic-reference",[8461]="Deadwood of the North\031Nafien would like you to kill 6 Deadwood Den Watchers, 6 Deadwood Avengers, and 6 Deadwood Shamans.  Return to him in northern Felwood near the entrance to Timbermaw Hold.\03115395\03115395\031\031\0311769\031classic-reference",[8462]="Speak to Nafien\031Travel north along the main road in Felwood and speak with the furbolg named Nafien.  He stands guard outside the entrance to Timbermaw Hold.\03111554\03115395\0318460\031\031361\031classic-reference",[8464]="Winterfall Activity\031Salfa wants you to kill 8 Winterfall Shaman, 8 Winterfall Den Watchers, and 8 Winterfall Ursa.  Salfa is located just outside the entrance to Timbermaw Hold in Winterspring.\03111556\03111556\031\0318469\0311769\031classic-reference",[8465]="Speak to Salfa\031Travel through Timbermaw Hold and exit into Winterspring.  Speak with Salfa, who stands guard outside the entrance to Timbermaw Hold.\03115395\03111556\0318461\031\031361\031classic-reference",[8466]="Feathers for Grazle\031Some of the Deadwood furbolgs wear a distinctive headdress that may be used as a means of proof in thinning their numbers. Bring me a feather from any headdresses you acquire; for every set of five you bring me, you will earn recognition amongst the Timbermaw.\03111554\03111554\0318460\031\031361\031classic-reference",[8467]="Feathers for Nafien\031Some of the Deadwood furbolgs wear a distinctive headdress that may be used as a means of proof in thinning their numbers. Bring me a feather from any headdresses you acquire; for every set of five you bring me, you will earn recognition amongst the Timbermaw.\03115395\03115395\0318461\031\031361\031classic-reference",[8469]="Beads for Salfa\031The Winterfall are known to carry spirit beads to ward against foul spirits. These beads have clearly failed in their purpose, as the Winterfall themselves are the agents of corruption. Bring to me these spirit beads from fallen Winterfall furbolgs; for every set of five you bring me, you will earn recognition amongst the Timbermaw.\03111556\03111556\0318464\031\031361\031classic-reference",[847]="Guile of the Raptor\031Speak with Tor'gan.\0312792\0312706\031702\031\03145\031classic-reference",[8470]="Deadwood Ritual Totem\031Take the Deadwood Ritual Totem inside Timbermaw Hold and see if one of the furbolgs there will find a use for the item.  The Timbermaw will not speak with you unless you are of Neutral reputation or greater with them.\031\03111558\031\031\031361\031classic-reference",[8471]="Winterfall Ritual Totem\031Take the Winterfall Ritual Totem inside Timbermaw Hold and see if one of the furbolgs there will find a use for the item.  The Timbermaw will not speak with you unless you are of Neutral reputation or greater with them.\031\03111558\031\031\031618\031classic-reference",[848]="Fungal Spores\031Bring 4 Fungal Spores to Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads.\0313390\0313390\031\031853\03117\031classic-reference",[8481]="The Root of All Evil\031Plant the Demon Summoning Torch in the mouth of High Chief Winterfall's cave in the Winterfall furbolg village.  Defeat the demon and retrieve the Essence of Xandivious for Gorn One Eye in Timbermaw Hold.\03111555\03111555\031\031\0311769\031classic-reference",[8484]="The Brokering of Peace\031Bring the Timbermaw Offering of Peace to King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge.\03111555\0312784\0318481\031\0311769\031classic-reference",[8485]="The Brokering of Peace\031Bring the Timbermaw Offering of Peace to Thrall in Orgrimmar.\03111555\0314949\0318481\031\0311769\031classic-reference",[849]="Revenge of Gann\031Destroy the flying machine at Bael Modan and return to Gann Stonespire.\0313341\0313341\031846\031\03117\031classic-reference",[8492]="The Alliance Needs Copper Bars!\031Bring 20 Copper Bars to Sergeant Stonebrow at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\03115383\03115383\031\0318493\031-365\031classic-reference",[8493]="The Alliance Needs More Copper Bars!\031Bring 20 copper bars to Sergeant Stonebrow at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\03115383\03115383\0318492\031\031-365\031classic-reference",[8494]="The Alliance Needs Iron Bars!\031Bring 20 Iron Bars to Corporal Carnes at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\03115431\03115431\031\0318495\031-365\031classic-reference",[8495]="The Alliance Needs More Iron Bars!\031Bring 20 iron bars to Corporal Carnes at the airfield in Dun Morogh.\03115431\03115431\0318494\031\031-365\031classic-reference",[8496]="Bandages for the Field\031Bring 30 Heavy Runecloth Bandages, 30 Heavy Silk Bandages and 30 Heavy Mageweave Bandages to Windcaller Proudhorn at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing X in order to complete this quest.\031\03115191\031\031\0311377\031classic-reference",[8497]="Desert Survival Kits\031Bring 4 Globes of Water, 4 Powerful Anti-Venom and 4 Smoked Desert Dumplings to Calandrath at the inn in Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing I in order to complete this quest.\031\03115174\031\031\0311377\031classic-reference",[8498]="Twilight Battle Orders\031Obtain the Twilight Battle Orders and bring them Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus.  You must also bring Tactical Task Briefing X in order to complete this quest.\031\03115181\031\031\0311377\031classic-reference",[8499]="The Alliance Needs Thorium Bars!\031Bring 20 Thorium Bars to Dame Twinbraid at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\03115432\03115432\031\0318500\031-365\031classic-reference",[85]="Lost Necklace\031Speak with Billy Maclure.\031246\031247\031\03186\03112\031classic-reference",[850]="Kolkar Leaders\031Bring Barak'